					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quasibenevolence" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5140935); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5140935&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607201031" alt="Quasibenevolence" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5140935)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quasibenevolence" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5140935); return false;" >Quasibenevolence</a></span> <span class="odate time_1549096615 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Feb 2019 08:36</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4139018">
									

<p>Feudalism to kleptocracy is no long walk so there are amusing themes here, but the implementation is problematic. This is a completely uncontained Keter that kills people — at the very least its classification as Euclid is wrong. I get that the point is that it’s amusing for the cliche contest, but it’s a gaping wound in reality that the Foundation would either contain or be forced to neutralize, and that’s a bigger deal than the central gag.</p>
<p>Keep in mind, not everyone is in on the gag. If the feudalists try to employ violence against someone not infected by the cognitohazard and the victim fights back successfully, you’ll have a lot of dead bodies and complete containment breach, followed quickly by more dead bodies. And how have authorities not arrested all concerned yet?</p>
<p>For me, the diplomacy log is far less important than those plot holes, so when I got that instead of an explanation, I became distinctly unhappy with the writing.</p>

							</div>

								
					
